6. Variable Declaration and Initialization
There are two important terms:

Declaration:

- Declaring a variable without assigning a value to it.

Example:
var name;
console.log(name);


Output:
undefined


Initialization:

- Assigning a value to a variable.

Example:
var name = "Somu";


Declaration and Initialization in Different Lines
var name;
name = "Somu";

console.log(name);


Output:
Somu


Declaration and Initialization in the Same Line
var name = "Somu";

console.log(name);


Output:
Somu


Reinitialization
Assigning a new value to an already declared variable.

Example:
var name = "Somu";
name = "Ravi";

console.log(name);


Output:
Ravi


Redeclaration
Declaring the same variable again using the same declaration keyword.

Example:
var name = "Somu";
var name = "Ravi";

console.log(name);


Output:
Ravi


Note: name is deprecated as a variable name in some browser contexts because it is also a global property. Prefer using names such as userName.
